{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-51034",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "As $x$ approaches $5$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty $, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is not defined for $x>5,$ and consequently, we cannot approach $x=5$ from the right. So we have \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n  \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
